# ============================================================================
# A note on what is NOT here
# ============================================================================
# This file applies to every repository on the machine, so it only lists
# patterns that are unambiguous: OS cruft, editor state, credentials, and
# artifacts named by extension.
#
# Bare generic directory names are deliberately left out, even though the
# upstream Python and Node templates include them: build, dist, out, target,
# lib, lib64, var, env, ENV, parts, sdist, wheels, eggs, develop-eggs,
# downloads, coverage, logs.
#
# In a project's own .gitignore those are scoped to that project. Here they
# would hide real source: `lib/` once made bootstrap/lib/packages.sh in this
# very repo invisible to git, with no error and nothing in `git status`.
#
# Put them in each project's .gitignore instead. To check what is hiding a
# file:
#
#   git check-ignore -v <path>
#
# Global gitignore patterns for all repositories
# This file should be symlinked to ~/.gitignore_global

